    "seat_scheme": "mixed",
    "term_length": 2,
    "stagger_pattern": "No stagger - all 13 seats (3 at-large + 2 in each of 5 districts) are elected concurrently at the biennial town election in November of ODD years (2021, 2023, 2025). The inaugural council elected 2018-11-06 under the 2018 charter served a TRANSITIONAL 3-YEAR term (ballot printed 'COUNCILOR (3 years)'), seated 2018-12-03 and running to 2022-01-03; there was therefore NO council election in 2019 (the 2019-11-05 town election carried School Committee, Housing Authority, Library Trustees and Elector of the Oliver Smith Will only) and none in any even year.",
    "mayor_selection": "none - Amherst has NO mayor. The Council elects a President from among its own members (Charter Sec. 2.2(b)); the Town Manager is an appointed administrator, not an elected official.",
    "election_month": "November (odd years)",
